TEXT 328 -8 Left 2 ;From symmetrical components textbook different faults:\n \n1phase+Earthfault: with U0=63500 Z0=R0+j*X0=0.245+j*1.458   ZM=ZG=ZL=0.1+j*0.375 \n \nI1=3*U0 / (Z0+ZM+ZG) = 3*110000/sqrt(3) / ( (0.245+j*1.458) + (0.1+j*0.375) + (0.1+j*0.375) )\nI1=85kA I1peak=85kA*sqrt(2)=120kA\n \n2 phase without earth: impedances see above\n \nI2:  j*sqrt(3)*U0/(ZM+ZG) = j*sqrt(3)*63500/((0.1+j*0.375)+(0.1+j*0.375))\nI2: 141kA\nI3=-I2\n \n2 phase with earth:  impedances see above\n \nI2: (-j*U0*sqrt(3)*(Z0+(1+a2)*ZG)/x) with a2=(-0.5-j*0.866) and x=Z0*ZM+Z0*ZG+ZM*ZG\nI2=142kA\nI3: (j*U0*sqrt(3)*(Z0+(1+a)*ZG)/x) with a=(-0.5+j*0.866)\nI3=147kA\nIE=I2+I3= (-j*U0*sqrt(3)*(Z0+(1+a2)*ZG)/x) + (j*U0*sqrt(3)*(Z0+(1+a)*ZG)/x) = 57kA (vectorial added !!)\n \n3 phase without earth:  impedances see above\n \nI=U0/ZM=164kA
TEXT 328 232 Left 2 ;For the case of double earth fault with open star point see file\n1sysSymmetric_shorted_2earth.asc\nHINT: See also wxmaxima files (.wxmx) with the same names\n in the same directory
TEXT 512 -144 Left 2 ;Computation RE,X0,XE: see Flosdorf/Hilgarth page 38\nRE=Ker*frequence = Pi*1e-4*50=0.05/km\nXE=(X0-XL)/3   \nX0=3*mue*frequency*ln(deltae/sqrt3(0.779*r*dgmi*dgmi)=    (sqrt3=third radix)\n  3*4*pi*1e-7*50*ln(deltae/sqrt3(0.779*0.01m*3m*3m))=  \n  = 1.456mohm/m = 1.456ohm/km => XE=(X0-XL)/3=(1.458-0.375)/3 = 0.36ohm/km
